Id: boot010i
Severity: INFO
Category: boot
Check: check_secureboot

The system started from a legacy BIOS (or UEFI's compatibility mode),
not UEFI, so Secure Boot cannot be on: nothing checks the boot loader
or the kernel before they run. Machines from the last ten years can
usually boot in UEFI mode, but switching an installed system means
converting its disk to GPT and installing a UEFI boot loader. On a
virtual machine, choose UEFI firmware (OVMF) when creating it.
